  "root_cause_analysis": "Turn 1 shows the model requesting user input for fuel tank capacity instead of proceeding with fillFuelTank immediately. However, Turn 2 recovered by executing fillFuelTank(35) and gallon_to_liter(50) correctly, suggesting the clarification was conversational padding rather than a blocking issue. Turn 3 shows redundant startEngine calls (4 total) with interleaved lockDoors and pressBrakePedal, violating delta2 (execute prerequisite sequence once per turn), yet the evaluation still passed because final state was correct.",
  "correct_approach": "Per delta4, invoke fillFuelTank immediately with calculated fuel amount without requesting clarification. Per delta2, execute pressBrakePedal → lockDoors → startEngine exactly once in sequence during startup, not interleaved or repeated. The model should have inferred the 50-gallon capacity from context or backend response rather than deferring.",
  "key_insight": "Evaluation passed because state outcomes matched ground truth despite procedural inefficiencies (redundant calls, deferred operations, conversational delays). The model's tool invocations were functionally correct, but violated playbook deltas around immediate execution and single-invocation-per-turn discipline."
